From 436eb6c13565b8114de5ec3041a1bb198c7ca45c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:34:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban workspace_source: the unpublished_workspace
 park refusal names the publish refusal

Symptom (LIVE proof of t_01a1cc30806b0e62, card t_01a1d5b1c1798e2a on hermes-worker-4): `kanban_schedule` on a
worktree card with publish_on_park enabled was refused with only `unpublished_workspace: commit and push the task
branch before parking, or add UNPUBLISHED_WORK_REASON=...`. The real cause, `source_clone_unregistered`, went only
to a `workspace_source_publish_refused` event, so the agent could not tell the fix was registering the clone. It
parked with UNPUBLISHED_WORK_REASON and the card stayed host-bound.

Why: the preflight (outer) turns every PublishRefused into a `retained` receipt and an event; the publication guard
(inner) then refuses on the unpublished branch with fixed text and never sees the refusal.

Fix:
- kanban_source_preflight scopes a per-(task, run) refusal list in a ContextVar around the ending; compute_receipt
  records each PublishRefused there; `refusal_hint(task_id, run_id)` renders the last one.
- The guard's `unpublished_workspace` message appends
  ` (workspace_source publish refused: <code>: <detail>[; <fix>])`. For `source_clone_unregistered` the fix names
  `kanban.workspace_source.clones` ({"<owner>/<name>": "<clone root>"}).
- prove_origin's `source_clone_unregistered` detail names the worktree's own clone root (the git common dir's
  parent), e.g. the second checkout ~/code/coworld-terraform vs the registered ~/code/_src/coworld-terraform.
No behaviour change: sibling clones stay fail-closed (not auto-registered); receipts and events are unchanged.

Proof:
- RED on base (source files reverted, new tests kept): test_unpublished_park_refusal_names_the_publish_refusal fails
  (`'workspace_source publish refused: source_clone_unregistered:' in 'unpublished_workspace: ...'`).
- GREEN: test_kanban_source_publish.py 77 passed; with test_kanban_publication_recovery.py,
  test_kanban_workspace_publication.py, test_kanban_source_resolver.py 140 passed. scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
- test_publish_refusal_hint_is_scoped_to_the_preflighted_run kills the task/run scope mutants; the
  publish_on_park=False test pins the unchanged message when no publish was attempted.
